    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is an array and what are its operations?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "An array is a fixed-size collection of elements of the same type. Key operations include access O(1), search O(n), insert/delete O(n)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Arrays store elements contiguously in memory. Access by index is O(1). Linear search is O(n). Insertion/deletion requires shifting elements. Dynamic arrays (List<T>, ArrayList) provide automatic resizing."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Array Operations",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};\nint first = nums[0];  // O(1) access\n// Insert at index 2: O(n) - must shift elements"
      }
    },
    {
